<BaseLayout title="Front brake pads">
  <h1>Front brake pad replacement</h1>
  <p>This guide records a planning and inspection workflow for the front brakes on the 2021 S60. Brake configurations can vary by engine, trim, wheel package, market, and option code. T5, T6, T8, and Polestar Engineered should not be assumed to share pad shapes or rotor dimensions. Confirm the VIN-specific brake package, pad shape, rotor dimensions, caliper, and hardware before ordering parts.</p>

  <div class="note"><strong>Safety-critical work:</strong> Brakes are essential to vehicle control. If you do not have the correct tools, service data, lifting equipment, or experience, have the work performed by a qualified technician. Never drive the car if the pedal is soft, a leak is present, or a brake warning remains.</div>

  <h2>Configuration differences</h2>
  <p>Brake package is not reliably identified by trim badge alone. Performance-oriented variants may use different calipers, discs, pads, and wheel-clearance requirements. Rear brake service may also involve the electronic parking brake and a prescribed service mode. Use the exact axle-specific Volvo procedure.</p>

  <h2>Parts to confirm before starting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Correct front pad set for the VIN and brake package.</li>
    <li>Any specified retaining springs, clips, guide-pin boots, caps, or replacement fasteners.</li>
    <li>Rotor condition and minimum-thickness specification.</li>
    <li>Correct brake lubricant for the specific contact points; keep all lubricant off friction surfaces.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tools and preparation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Correct wheel-removal tools and a calibrated torque wrench.</li>
    <li>Rated jack and jack stands, wheel chocks, and a stable level work area.</li>
    <li>Caliper support hook or other suitable support; never let the caliper hang from the flexible brake hose.</li>
    <li>Brake-cleaning product intended for brake components, eye protection, gloves, and suitable dust control.</li>
    <li>VIN-specific Volvo repair instructions and all required special tools.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Work sequence — overview</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Verify the correct parts and service procedure before lifting the car. Compare the new pads and hardware with the removed components.</li>
    <li>Park on a firm, level surface, secure the vehicle, and lift/support it only at the specified points. Remove the wheel.</li>
    <li>Inspect the caliper, brake hose, rotor, pad wear pattern, guide hardware, and dust boots before disassembly. Stop if there is leakage, binding, corrosion damage, or a damaged hose.</li>
    <li>Remove the caliper hardware using the specified tools and procedure. Support the caliper so no load is placed on the hose.</li>
    <li>Remove the pads and inspect the carrier/contact points. Clean only as permitted by the service procedure; do not damage boots or sealing surfaces.</li>
    <li>Retract the front caliper piston using the correct press tool and the specified method. Do not twist or force the piston. Monitor the brake-fluid reservoir so it does not overflow.</li>
    <li>Install the specified hardware and pads in the correct orientation. Reassemble using new fasteners where Volvo requires them and use VIN-specific torque values.</li>
    <li>Reinstall the wheel and tighten fasteners using the correct sequence and torque specification.</li>
    <li>Before moving the car, press the brake pedal repeatedly until it is firm. Check fluid level and inspect for leaks. Follow the pad manufacturer's/Volvo's bedding instructions.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Inspection and stop conditions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Replace or professionally assess rotors that are below minimum thickness, cracked, badly scored, or heat-damaged.</li>
    <li>Investigate uneven pad wear rather than simply fitting new pads; a sticking guide or piston may be the cause.</li>
    <li>Replace damaged guide boots/caps with the correct kit. Confirm lubricant compatibility and placement from the service instructions.</li>
    <li>If the pedal does not become firm, fluid leaks, the car pulls, or a warning appears, do not drive it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Vehicle-specific job record</h2>
  <p>Record the pad brand and part number, hardware kit, rotor measurements, odometer, date, any replaced boots/caps, and the source of each torque value. Do not copy torque values from another S60 or from a generic brake guide.</p>

  <h2>Official service information</h2>
  <p>The public owner's manual does not provide the complete brake-pad replacement procedure, fastener torque values, or variant-specific service steps. Obtain the VIN-specific procedure from <a href="https://www.volvotechinfo.com/">Volvo Technical Information</a> before starting. The independent diagram and planning notes on this page are not a substitute for that procedure.</p>
